ld #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]offclock_types.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/offclock_types.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-hc[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-hc/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-cli resolver, lints, shared vectors, and contract docs[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]clock-type-filter[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]clock-type-filter: parse the `offclock_types` key, extract a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog-free effective-type helper shared with type suggestions, give [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]HomeResolver type rules, apply the nearest-declaration rule in the clock[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]walk, add the shadowed lint and key-naming messages, extend the shared [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]clock vectors with a `config` member and the new cases, and update every[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-cli doc that states the clock rule.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]gcal list preview and running-entry re-stamps on naming[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]clock-surfaces[dim] · [dim][/dim]after clock-type-filter[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]clock-surfaces: give the `bob gcal list` probe line `\\[type:: MEET]` so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preview matches sync; make `bob capture-pomodoro-name` and capture's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`#type` relocations that rename or move a running entry recompute that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]entry's clock key in the same write; document that every other retype is[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]corrected at close.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob types rename and split cover offclock_types lists[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]type-rename-coverage[dim] · [dim][/dim]after clock-type-filter[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]type-rename-coverage: `bob types rename` rewrites matching [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`offclock_types` items in flow, block, and scalar form inside its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]existing previewed transaction, removing duplicates when two types [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]merge; `split` leaves the lists alone and counts them in its leftover [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]warning; update docs/task-types.md.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-plugins clock mirror and vector copies[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]plugin-mirror[dim] · [dim][/dim]after clock-type-filter[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugin-mirror: in the bob-plugins linked repo, teach bob-ledger-tools' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`taskEffectiveClockResolution` the same `offclock_types` rules with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]type helper that also handles closed tasks, copy the shared vectors byte[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for byte into both plugin fixture directories, make the test harnesses [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]honor `config`, update plugin docs, rebuild, test, and run `bob plugins [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync`.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Decision record and glossary updates[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-records[dim] · [dim][/dim]after clock-type-filter, clock-surfaces, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]type-rename-coverage[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-records: through /sase_memory_write, add the new decisions [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]strand, mark off-clock